{"fileId":"1gVM2xPQDwPJgo6Iynb-A9sG7ZXdtBOFT","sourceSha256":"6e9189a12b6170c936871d0605a2def9adbc1fc155c84f6543ee39a0d84d7c55","blocks":{"d1b54e8c3ce6710f51f8":{"type":"paragraph","page":4,"text":"A conditional sentence is a type of sentence that tells a condition and","bbox":[108.0199966430664,607.4459838867188,539.18359375,621.4500122070312]},"5eacfd6f2ed88e9c0971":{"type":"paragraph","page":4,"text":"its result. It is composed of a main clause (independent clause) and a subordinate clause (dependent clause) which is also known as the if-clause.","bbox":[72.0250015258789,621.64599609375,539.4979248046875,649.8500366210938]},"675d9f003bb1046090bb":{"type":"heading","page":4,"text":"What is the function of Conditional Sentence Type 2?","bbox":[72.0250015258789,657.4459838867188,414.0,671.426025390625]},"3368fac26f3b849684eb":{"type":"paragraph","page":4,"text":"The second type of conditional sentence expresses dreams or unreal","bbox":[108.0199966430664,679.0459594726562,539.3036499023438,693.0499877929688]},"65ef9747f9be80191d08":{"type":"paragraph","page":4,"text":"situations in the present or in the future. It is used in the following situations:","bbox":[72.0250015258789,693.2459716796875,539.6200561523438,707.25]},"9c61d38a1f1b72cbe8ca":{"type":"paragraph","page":4,"text":"1) for an occurrence or result of a condition that is impossible to fulfill;","bbox":[144.0500030517578,714.865966796875,539.229736328125,743.0800170898438]},"19cf0d6d74ca8959c074":{"type":"paragraph","page":5,"text":"• If I had a superpower, I could go anywhere in just a second. (The condition “had a superpower” is fictional and cannot be fulfilled.) • Would you invite me for a cruise If you owned a private yacht? (The condition is contrary to the fact and unlikely to happen) • You are just a student. If you were a doctor, you could help to treat the COVID-19 patients. (The condition could be met but not possible to achieve.)","bbox":[162.0500030517578,71.97003173828125,543.2200317382812,186.8099822998047]},"a83aca1da53234b20d48":{"type":"paragraph","page":5,"text":"2) to give advice • I would not stop studying if I were you. • If I were you, I would accept the challenge.","bbox":[144.0500030517578,200.9459991455078,437.55999755859375,244.74998474121094]},"e1d6c673af1a228b6aa0":{"type":"heading","page":5,"text":"What is the structure of Conditional Sentence Type 2?","bbox":[72.0250015258789,258.7460021972656,419.0099792480469,272.7259826660156]},"cf0735194cb5828ba52c":{"type":"table","rows":[["If-Clause","Result-Clause"],["If + subject + V2 (past form)","Subject + (would, could, might + V1 (base/present form)"],["Affirmative If I noticed the kidnappers, If we submitted our project on time, Negative If she attended webinars, If you reminded me earlier, Interrogative If you were a millionaire, If you were forgiven,","I would call the policemen. our teacher could give us a good grade. she might not be left behind. I wouldn’t attend the party. would you share your wealth to others? wouldn’t you forgive other too?"]],"bbox":[72.1750020980835,287.2033284505208,535.4199981689453,457.76666259765625],"text":"If-Clause Result-Clause If + subject + V2 (past form) Subject + (would, could, might + V1 (base/present form) Affirmative If I noticed the kidnappers, If we submitted our project on time, Negative If she attended webinars, If you reminded me earlier, Interrogative If you were a millionaire, If you were forgiven, I would call the policemen. our teacher could give us a good grade. she might not be left behind. I wouldn’t attend the party. would you share your wealth to others? wouldn’t you forgive other too?","page":5},"8dc0f91c82a8450990a6":{"type":"paragraph","page":5,"text":"Note:","bbox":[72.0250015258789,472.1960144042969,112.86000061035156,486.20001220703125]},"634fde739e2a5f6aa352":{"type":"paragraph","page":5,"text":"Conditional sentences can be written in two ways:","bbox":[108.0199966430664,486.1960144042969,409.7699890136719,500.20001220703125]},"49d1de696a9592a6740f":{"type":"paragraph","page":5,"text":"• If it did not rain, the children would play outside. (use a comma {,} after the if-clause)","bbox":[126.05000305175781,514.4700317382812,441.19000244140625,543.2300415039062]},"94608125563ba2426e31":{"type":"paragraph","page":5,"text":"OR","bbox":[252.0800018310547,543.4259643554688,278.91998291015625,557.4299926757812]},"3e6e78235c033441ab1a":{"type":"paragraph","page":5,"text":"• The children would play outside if it did not rain.","bbox":[126.05000305175781,557.4700317382812,439.760009765625,572.2300415039062]},"459baa1307daf510b31c":{"type":"heading","page":5,"text":"(no need to use a comma if the main clause comes first)","bbox":[144.0500030517578,572.2260131835938,500.8299865722656,586.2060546875]},"f992acc922bf3eb46e64":{"type":"paragraph","page":5,"text":"B. Directions: Match column A with column B. Write the letter only.","bbox":[72.0250015258789,677.64599609375,483.7900085449219,691.6500244140625]},"304e83b9e3c1590ce7a5":{"type":"table","rows":[["COLUMN A","COLUMN B"],["1. If we took good care of our environment,","A. you would pass the exam."],["2. If you listened carefully,","B. you would appreciate the lecture."]],"bbox":[72.1750020980835,700.8833414713541,535.4199981689453,758.8416341145834],"text":"COLUMN A COLUMN B 1. If we took good care of our environment, A. you would pass the exam. 2. If you listened carefully, B. you would appreciate the lecture.","page":5},"2d49f91ee657857be07e":{"type":"table","rows":[["3. If they were rich,","C. we would have clean air to breathe."],["4. If you studied harder,","D. I wouldn’t wake up late."],["5. If I slept early last night,","E. they would donate PPEs for the front liners."]],"bbox":[72.1750020980835,72.15999348958333,535.4199981689453,144.09663899739584],"text":"3. If they were rich, C. we would have clean air to breathe. 4. If you studied harder, D. I wouldn’t wake up late. 5. If I slept early last night, E. they would donate PPEs for the front liners.","page":6},"8db7c54078f34d75e13b":{"type":"paragraph","page":6,"text":"A. Directions: Read the text inside the box then do the activity below. Choose the correct form of the verb inside the parenthesis.","bbox":[72.0250015258789,157.3460235595703,539.169677734375,185.3500213623047]},"963f01161e3176347091":{"type":"paragraph","page":6,"text":"Tony is a junior high school student. He has a lot of dreams for his community. He imagines what would happen if he were a barangay chairman.","bbox":[83.42500305175781,203.74598693847656,536.6200561523438,233.15000915527344]},"98e99547dc2c082bfa90":{"type":"paragraph","page":6,"text":"6. If I (am, were) a barangay chairman, I (will encourage, would encourage) my constituents to stay at home during the pandemic. 7. If my constituents (need, needed) food supplies: I (will tell, would tell) my staff to have it delivered weekly to them. 8. If food supplies (are, were) not enough, I (will give, would give) cash money. 9. If my office (can’t, couldn’t) afford to extend financial aid to all, I (will solicit, would solicit) from the national government organizations. 10. My community (will be, would be) safe from the virus if the people (stay, stayed) at home.","bbox":[90.0250015258789,251.3460235595703,539.34765625,424.8000183105469]},"147ccaae1917a8b98d7d":{"type":"paragraph","page":6,"text":"B. Directions: Complete the following sentences: 11. My mom would buy me a new cellphone if _______________________. 12. If I had a younger brother, ______________________________________. 13. _____________________________________ if you were an astronaut. 14. If I lived in the palace, _________________________________________. 15. Online classes would be possible, ________________________________.","bbox":[72.0250015258789,439.1960144042969,513.5900268554688,569.2300415039062]},"8cb2ae34512cf7f55e48":{"type":"paragraph","page":6,"text":"Directions: Express what you had learned in this lesson by completing the sentences below.","bbox":[72.0250015258789,680.0459594726562,539.1298217773438,708.0499877929688]},"243e3591ba51c1b958e4":{"type":"paragraph","page":6,"text":"1. Conditional sentence is","bbox":[72.0250015258789,722.2659912109375,228.01309204101562,736.27001953125]},"47e56cc0ab89041052d7":{"type":"paragraph","page":7,"text":"2. The second type of conditional sentence expresses","bbox":[72.0250015258789,85.91596984863281,389.57000732421875,99.91996765136719]},"ef18c61634c3dcea4199":{"type":"paragraph","page":7,"text":"3. This type of conditional sentences is formed by","bbox":[72.0250015258789,142.3159942626953,365.7729187011719,156.3199920654297]},"f40e3c2f0dcfae61b727":{"type":"paragraph","page":7,"text":"4. The two basic parts of conditional sentences are: ___________________________________; and ____________________________________","bbox":[72.0250015258789,198.74598693847656,535.8099975585938,226.9499969482422]},"46447812a759e08cdc93":{"type":"paragraph","page":7,"text":"A. Directions: Answer the following using conditionals type II.","bbox":[72.0250015258789,339.3760070800781,446.989990234375,353.3800048828125]},"dd08a6cf5e9e0f967d31":{"type":"paragraph","page":7,"text":"What would happen if:","bbox":[72.0250015258789,367.5660095214844,212.72000122070312,381.57000732421875]},"07f5cfc00e8636c6a21d":{"type":"paragraph","page":7,"text":"1. there were no vaccine for COVID-19","bbox":[72.0250015258789,395.7960205078125,324.739990234375,409.8000183105469]},"475ce8ae2b53fd358a8e":{"type":"paragraph","page":7,"text":"2. more people were hopeless","bbox":[72.0250015258789,437.9960021972656,270.5199890136719,452.0]},"a4bb2f005c8bb26d2298":{"type":"paragraph","page":7,"text":"3. nobody would lead our country","bbox":[72.0250015258789,480.1960144042969,297.3399963378906,494.20001220703125]},"9b43e002c0d438a5d74f":{"type":"paragraph","page":7,"text":"4. schools had virtual classrooms","bbox":[72.0250015258789,522.6160278320312,295.5400085449219,536.6200561523438]},"0627b19824393fa6346f":{"type":"paragraph","page":7,"text":"5. the sea ran dry","bbox":[72.0250015258789,564.8159790039062,203.11000061035156,578.8200073242188]},"ee4c7d9d557a5c97f8a3":{"type":"paragraph","page":7,"text":"B. Directions: Express your insights on the following situations using type II conditional sentences.","bbox":[72.0250015258789,607.0459594726562,539.2637939453125,635.25]},"32bf017ec79cbc3f6b24":{"type":"paragraph","page":7,"text":"6. If you qualified for a scholarship abroad, what school would you choose and what course would you like to take?","bbox":[90.0250015258789,648.2228393554688,539.4407958984375,675.1599731445312]},"a83ae9f40449999bedf8":{"type":"paragraph","page":8,"text":"7. If you were the only survivor in an island after a plane crash or a shipwreck, how could you survive?","bbox":[90.0250015258789,71.90281677246094,539.0994262695312,98.82997131347656]},"18d05a73b35d11e9232c":{"type":"paragraph","page":8,"text":"8. If you were the president, how would you solve the emerging problems or social issues in our country?","bbox":[90.0250015258789,193.3460235595703,539.3217163085938,221.5499725341797]},"6416d2ff950d3fa996f6":{"type":"paragraph","page":8,"text":"9. What would you do if you were a frontliner?","bbox":[90.0250015258789,317.1659851074219,372.57000732421875,331.16998291015625]},"bcde63c154c7b7883809":{"type":"paragraph","page":8,"text":"10. Your friend has a health problem. What advice would you give him to stay","bbox":[72.0250015258789,426.9960021972656,543.4200439453125,441.0]},"acb68759bc6234c49ae3":{"type":"paragraph","page":8,"text":"healthy.","bbox":[107.43000030517578,442.1960144042969,158.88999938964844,456.20001220703125]},"2fdc2c253421ce9945c3":{"type":"paragraph","page":8,"text":"B. Directions: Write a letter of advice using type 2 conditional sentences. (2 pts.-expression of ideas; 3 pts.- correct usage)","bbox":[72.0250015258789,555.4159545898438,507.5899963378906,583.4299926757812]},"f3f1141067f4db8da777":{"type":"paragraph","page":8,"text":"You were Luisa. Your friend Tessa got addicted to online games and","bbox":[108.0199966430664,597.615966796875,539.0836181640625,611.6199951171875]},"46ae958de4a3ff0065df":{"type":"paragraph","page":8,"text":"almost forgot school and even had a weight loss because of not eating food on time. Write a letter of advice. Start your letter with:","bbox":[72.0250015258789,611.8460083007812,539.4117431640625,639.8500366210938]},"6b9cd6866ce223de5216":{"type":"paragraph","page":8,"text":"Dear Tessa,","bbox":[108.0199966430664,640.0459594726562,180.69000244140625,654.0499877929688]},"2c5937964b1db7b14ea8":{"type":"paragraph","page":8,"text":"If I were you _____________________________________________________","bbox":[144.0500030517578,654.0459594726562,539.6200561523438,668.0499877929688]},"0513273fbd4df05f5813":{"type":"paragraph","page":8,"text":"Your friend, Luisa","bbox":[432.1300048828125,738.6709594726562,505.7900085449219,766.6749877929688]},"2314023c41cbebff450f":{"type":"heading","page":9,"text":"A. Directions: Choose the correct form of the verb that will best complete","bbox":[72.0250015258789,139.7260284423828,539.148681640625,153.70602416992188]},"92f76b1d7f2f82fdf6d8":{"type":"heading","page":9,"text":"each conditional sentence below. Write the letter only.","bbox":[72.0250015258789,154.9459991455078,420.2099914550781,168.92599487304688]},"19cfecbc8ee9a1654b15":{"type":"paragraph","page":9,"text":"1. My dad __________ a new car if he _________ enough money.","bbox":[90.0250015258789,177.9459991455078,460.19000244140625,191.9499969482422]},"4356c2b2b9bdd3c6992b":{"type":"paragraph","page":9,"text":"A. will buy, earn","bbox":[126.05000305175781,192.14601135253906,231.9199981689453,206.15000915527344]},"4deea95cd41fe2b824c9":{"type":"paragraph","page":9,"text":"C. would buy, earned","bbox":[288.1000061035156,192.14601135253906,417.57000732421875,206.15000915527344]},"43be08d67c9a8a1003d8":{"type":"paragraph","page":9,"text":"B. buy, earn","bbox":[126.05000305175781,206.14