":[108.0199966430664,211.3460235595703,539.08984375,281.780029296875]},"59a25ff464792323c83e":{"type":"paragraph","page":2,"text":"A. Directions: Write the letter that corresponds to the term described in each item.","bbox":[72.0250015258789,374.5660095214844,539.1697387695312,402.6000061035156]},"49de954eff9f0fc39351":{"type":"paragraph","page":2,"text":"A. past tense of the verb","bbox":[145.25,410.1960144042969,295.1399841308594,424.20001220703125]},"f6737d82821dbe8149a3":{"type":"paragraph","page":2,"text":"D. Conditional sentence","bbox":[361.32000732421875,410.1960144042969,509.3899841308594,424.20001220703125]},"36e2fc02746b29c4b59c":{"type":"paragraph","page":2,"text":"B. Main clause","bbox":[145.25,424.3960266113281,240.30999755859375,438.4000244140625]},"aa0b6d2ede2c852e8e94":{"type":"paragraph","page":2,"text":"E. Type II conditional","bbox":[361.32000732421875,424.3960266113281,493.989990234375,438.4000244140625]},"a9fd3d51efc8a1fa4156":{"type":"paragraph","page":2,"text":"C. Subordinate clause","bbox":[145.25,438.59600830078125,293.1399841308594,452.6000061035156]},"70db4777057da0f8b425":{"type":"paragraph","page":2,"text":"F. Result clause","bbox":[361.32000732421875,438.59600830078125,459.19000244140625,452.6000061035156]},"d37865fab7e8bad4c079":{"type":"paragraph","page":2,"text":"_____1. Sentence that deals with unreal situation in the present or in the future. _____2. A clause that tells the condition and known as the “if-clause.” _____3. A verb form that is to be used in the subordinate clause of a type 2","bbox":[72.0250015258789,460.7960205078125,543.4200439453125,503.0299987792969]},"21b6e39dad915c8bc431":{"type":"paragraph","page":2,"text":"conditional sentence.","bbox":[114.62000274658203,503.0259704589844,246.9199981689453,517.0299682617188]},"8fd4563fa00cb8437e90":{"type":"paragraph","page":2,"text":"_____4. One of the basic clauses in the conditional sentence that can stand by","bbox":[72.0250015258789,517.0259399414062,539.171630859375,53