15720783cbb1c":{"type":"paragraph","page":3,"text":"B. was cured","bbox":[108.0199966430664,451.59600830078125,188.2899932861328,465.6000061035156]},"aeb1b3c4c35fc6936b26":{"type":"paragraph","page":3,"text":"D. will be cured","bbox":[288.1000061035156,451.59600830078125,384.16998291015625,465.6000061035156]},"9612f2724d812a227116":{"type":"paragraph","page":3,"text":"13. What kind of condition is expressed in this sentence, “If I were rich, my","bbox":[72.0250015258789,479.7960205078125,539.2979125976562,493.8600158691406]},"4e9b9de7da53e245e8bd":{"type":"paragraph","page":3,"text":"life would change completely.” A. a general truth B. a realistic situation in the present or future C. an impossible situation in the present or future D. an impossible condition in the past","bbox":[114.62000274658203,494.0160217285156,407.3699951171875,564.2300415039062]},"391a339e7f991704ffd1":{"type":"paragraph","page":3,"text":"For item number 14 & 15 refer to this question.","bbox":[72.0250015258789,578.4259643554688,359.94000244140625,592.4299926757812]},"47d416d233da31982ee7":{"type":"paragraph","page":3,"text":"Which two sentences express a condition?","bbox":[108.0199966430664,606.64599609375,363.1600036621094,620.6500244140625]},"e69e08e49784c7c16403":{"type":"paragraph","page":3,"text":"A. My brother would buy a sports car if he won in the lottery. B. She’s a student whose academic performance is excellent. C. Because I woke up late, I was not able to catch the first trip. D. If she were mad at you, she would not invite you in her party.","bbox":[108.0199966430664,677.0459594726562,490.7900085449219,733.4700317382812]},"3d17342b749ab995423e":{"type":"paragraph","page":4,"text":"Directions: Express your thoughts by filling each box with your responses using Type 1 conditional sentences.","bbox":[72.0250015258789,146.52601623535156,514.6976928710938,175.74998474121094]},"7d7838180cf92ac5ff17":{"type":"paragraph","page":4,"text":"If the weather is sunny, ….","bbox":[104.62000274658203,194.3460235595703,267.1099853515625,208.3500213623047]},"4da903c4e763a60b15c6":{"type":"paragraph","page":4,"text":"I will buy a new bike if ….","bbox":[305.5,194.3460235595703,460.66998291015625,208.3500213623047]},"0f56ebba261671960704":{"type":"paragraph","page":4,"text":"You will be safe from COVID-19","bbox":[104.62000274658203,318.1659851074219,294.5199890136719,332.16998291015625]},"55e523ea78319b1fc61c":{"type":"paragraph","page":4,"text":"If the pandemic ends, ….","bbox":[305.5,318.1659851074219,455.989990234375,332.16998291015625]},"18a66a67574c45a57b1f":{"type":"paragraph","page":4,"text":"virus if ….","bbox":[104.62000274658203,332.166015625,168.88999938964844,346.1700134277344]},"a440b54a9473d51595fa":{"type":"paragraph","page":4,"text":"The previous lesson discussed the zero and the first conditional","bbox":[108.0199966430664,535.8159790039062,539.1917114257812,549.8200073242188]},"4b1476473de4d27351d9":{"type":"paragraph","page":4,"text":"sentences. We will surely have a lot of learnings in the succeeding lesson, let us now be familiar with the next type of Conditional Sentences, its second type.","bbox":[72.0250015258789,550.0259399414062,539.4518432617188,578.2300415039062]},"516375b788490957789e":{"type":"heading","page":4,"text":"What is a Conditional Sentence?","bbox":[72.0250015258789,586.0260009765625,280.3499755859375,600.0060424804688]}},"excerptBlocks":{"concepts:0":["a440b54a9473d51595fa","4b1476473de4d27351d9","516375b788490957789e","d1b54e8c3ce6710f51f8","5eacfd6f2ed88e9c0971","675d9f003bb1046090bb","3368fac26f3b849684eb","65ef9747f9be80191d08","9c61d38a1f1b72cbe8ca"],"concepts:1":["19cf0d6d74ca8959c074","a83aca1da53234b20d48","e1d6c673af1a228b6aa0","cf0735194cb5828ba52c","8dc0f91c82a8450990a6","634fde739e2a5f6aa352","49d1de696a9592a6740f","94608125563ba2426e31","3e6e78235c033441ab1a","459baa1307daf510b31c"]},"games":[{"difficulty":"easy","answer":"conditional sentence","explanation":"A conditional sentence is a type of sentence 